902
00:45:30.020 --> 00:45:31.700
Well, I have to tell you something.
嗯，我得告诉你一件事。

903
00:45:31.960 --> 00:45:33.160
So all of this is happening.
所以这一切正在发生。

904
00:45:33.180 --> 00:45:39.860
While you have this scene between Pam and Jan going on, there is a scene between Bob,
当帕姆和简在演那场戏时，鲍勃、

905
00:45:39.860 --> 00:45:41.700
Vance, Phyllis, and Angela.
万斯、菲利斯和安吉拉之间也在演一场戏。

906
00:45:42.480 --> 00:45:47.520
So in the background where Toby is stretching, Angela's standing there, and Phyllis and Bob
在托比做拉伸的背景里，安吉拉站在那儿，菲利斯和鲍勃

907
00:45:47.520 --> 00:45:52.500
walk up, and Bob points to her shirt and says, oh, oh, is that the cat?
走了过来，鲍勃指着她的衬衫说，噢，噢，那是猫吗？

908
00:45:52.800 --> 00:45:56.700
And he turns to Phyllis and says, is that the one that Meredith...
然后他转向菲利斯说，那是梅雷迪思……的那只吗？

909
00:45:56.700 --> 00:45:59.460
And Phyllis quickly cuts him off and goes, no, no, no.
菲利斯赶紧打断他说，不，不，不。

910
00:45:59.880 --> 00:46:03.360
And then Angela spits on Bob.
然后安吉拉朝鲍勃吐了口水。

911
00:46:03.600 --> 00:46:04.080
What?
什么？

912
00:46:04.460 --> 00:46:05.840
And storms off.
然后气冲冲地走开了。

913
00:46:06.020 --> 00:46:07.920
What is happening in that scene?
那场戏里到底发生了什么？

914
00:46:07.920 --> 00:46:10.660
Did Meredith do something to one of your other cats?
梅雷迪思对你的其他猫做过什么吗？

915
00:46:10.860 --> 00:46:12.260
I have so many questions.
我有太多疑问了。

916
00:46:12.820 --> 00:46:14.920
What has Meredith done to one of her cats?
梅雷迪思到底对她的猫做过什么？

917
00:46:15.040 --> 00:46:18.320
It certainly might explain why Angela really does not like Meredith.
这确实能解释为什么安吉拉那么讨厌梅雷迪思。

918
00:46:19.200 --> 00:46:21.720
But man, Angela is...
但是天哪，安吉拉她……

919
00:46:21.720 --> 00:46:22.360
Talk about angry.
真是怒火中烧啊。

920
00:46:22.660 --> 00:46:24.320
She spits at Bob.
她竟然朝鲍勃吐口水。

921
00:46:25.140 --> 00:46:25.780
Wow.
哇。

922
00:46:26.160 --> 00:46:26.540
Yeah.
是啊。

923
00:46:27.780 --> 00:46:34.120
Well, now Michael welcomes everyone, and he gives a speech where he sort of warns
好吧，接着迈克尔欢迎了大家，他发表了一番演讲，算是警告

924
00:46:34.120 --> 00:46:36.700
everybody of the dangers of rabies.
所有人狂犬病的危险。

925
00:46:37.120 --> 00:46:41.880
In the background, then, Daryl is feeding a peanut to a squirrel.
背景里，达里尔正在喂松鼠吃花生。

926
00:46:43.120 --> 00:46:44.160
That was such...
那真是……

927
00:46:44.160 --> 00:46:45.760
That is such a random, funny joke.
那真是一个随机又好笑的梗。

928
00:46:45.940 --> 00:46:48.700
That's a very Simpsons-esque joke, if you ask me.
依我看，那是非常《辛普森一家》风格的笑话。

929
00:46:48.860 --> 00:46:49.760
I loved it.
我太喜欢了。

930
00:46:49.920 --> 00:46:52.840
And I love when Michael was like, stop, and he's like, but he's so happy.
我特别喜欢迈克尔说“停下”时，他回说“可它看起来好开心”。

931
00:46:55.260 --> 00:47:01.380
Well, then we have Elizabeth, the stripper, is back.
好吧，然后脱衣舞娘伊丽莎白又回来了。

932
00:47:01.600 --> 00:47:07.940
Jackie DeBotten, she walks in in this little nurse's outfit to present Michael with the giant
杰基·德博滕，她穿着那身小护士装走进来，要把那张写给“科学”的巨额

933
00:47:07.940 --> 00:47:10.360
check made out to science.
支票交给迈克尔。

934
00:47:10.700 --> 00:47:11.760
Just science.
就写着“科学”。

935
00:47:12.000 --> 00:47:12.100
Yeah.
是啊。

936
00:47:12.960 --> 00:47:14.780
$340 to science.
给科学捐了340美元。

937
00:47:15.020 --> 00:47:17.940
Just a piece of cardboard that cost $200 for nothing.
就为了这块花了200美元做的硬纸板，毫无意义。

938
00:47:18.640 --> 00:47:24.380
And when Michael sees Elizabeth in her outfit, he's like, oh my gosh, you went back for your
当迈克尔看到穿着那身行头的伊丽莎白时，他说，天哪，你回去

939
00:47:24.380 --> 00:47:24.800
degree.
拿学位了啊。

940
00:47:25.200 --> 00:47:25.360
Yeah.
是啊。

941
00:47:26.180 --> 00:47:26.680
Amazing.
太绝了。

942
00:47:26.840 --> 00:47:28.720
Well, I have a little wardrobe tidbit.
好吧，我有个关于服装的小花絮。

943
00:47:28.920 --> 00:47:30.440
I think I know your tidbit.
我想我知道你要说什么。

944
00:47:30.800 --> 00:47:31.460
Oh, really?
噢，真的吗？

945
00:47:31.620 --> 00:47:31.820
Go.
你说吧。

946
00:47:32.560 --> 00:47:32.920
All right.
好吧。

947
00:47:33.760 --> 00:47:40.320
Carrie told me that this nurse's outfit was custom made, and if you notice, she had to
嘉莉告诉我，这套护士装是定制的，如果你注意看，她必须

948
00:47:40.320 --> 00:47:44.100
make it a red circle with a white cross in the middle.
把它做成红底白十字的图案。

949
00:47:45.000 --> 00:47:51.520
And this is because the red cross does not like their symbol to be used for fictional content.
这是因为红十字会不喜欢他们的标志被用于虚构内容。

950
00:47:51.520 --> 00:47:55.200
So she could not have a red cross in a white circle.
所以她不能用白底红十字的标志。

951
00:47:55.440 --> 00:47:56.860
She had to invert it.
她不得不把它反过来穿。

952
00:47:57.520 --> 00:47:58.400
Yes, lady.
是的，女士。

953
00:47:58.760 --> 00:48:05.300
Well, do you know that that is the same costume that Angela Martin wore in season seven?
那么，你知道那和安吉拉·马丁在第七季穿的是同一套戏服吗？

954
00:48:06.220 --> 00:48:08.040
They saved that costume.
他们把那套戏服留下来了。

955
00:48:08.280 --> 00:48:12.860
Season seven, the Halloween episode where we have a costume conteSt.
第七季，我们举办戏服比赛的那集万圣节特辑。

956
00:48:13.360 --> 00:48:14.640
I wore that outfit.
我穿过那套衣服。

957
00:48:16.180 --> 00:48:16.660
What?
什么？

958
00:48:17.000 --> 00:48:17.480
Yep.
没错。

959
00:48:18.200 --> 00:48:23.880
I wore that outfit, the exact same one, and it was a little too big for me.
我穿过那套衣服，完全一模一样，对我来说稍微有点大。

960
00:48:23.880 --> 00:48:27.140
So I had to wear a little lace tank top underneath it.
所以我不得不在里面穿了一件蕾丝吊带背心。

961
00:48:27.440 --> 00:48:33.000
And, you know, we'll get to season seven, but they gave me the chicken cutlets to make everything
而且，你知道，我们之后会聊到第七季，但他们给了我胸垫来让一切

962
00:48:33.000 --> 00:48:33.640
a little bigger.
看起来丰满一点。

963
00:48:34.440 --> 00:48:34.920
Yep.
没错。

964
00:48:35.160 --> 00:48:35.840
Same costume.
同一套戏服。

965
00:48:37.000 --> 00:48:37.480
Wow.
哇。

966
00:48:38.220 --> 00:48:44.320
I guess in our Dunder Mifflin world, this is like a little costume that you could buy,
我想在我们的《办公室》世界里，这就像是一套你可以买到的戏服，

967
00:48:44.440 --> 00:48:44.780
I guess.
我想是吧。

968
00:48:44.920 --> 00:48:47.220
But Carrie Bennett told me that she made it.
但嘉莉·贝内特告诉我那是她亲手做的。

969
00:48:47.480 --> 00:48:48.420
There it is.
就在那儿。

970
00:48:49.060 --> 00:48:50.060
You're wearing it.
你正穿着它。

971
00:48:50.140 --> 00:48:53.880
And you can see it's this same white cross, the same hat.
你可以看到那是同一个白十字架，同一顶帽子。

972
00:48:53.920 --> 00:48:56.440
I just have a tank top because it's a little big.
我只是穿了件背心，因为它有点大。

973
00:48:56.860 --> 00:48:57.880
That is crazy.
那太疯狂了。

974
00:48:58.080 --> 00:48:58.500
I know.
我知道。

975
00:48:58.700 --> 00:48:59.040
Crazy.
疯狂。

976
00:48:59.040 --> 00:49:05.260
Well, speaking of crazy, Michael is now downing some fettuccine Alfredo.
说到疯狂，迈克尔现在正在狂吃意大利宽面。

977
00:49:05.420 --> 00:49:06.580
Just downing it.
简直是在狂吃。

978
00:49:06.700 --> 00:49:09.120
He's carbo-loading before the run.
他在跑步前进行碳水化合物储备。

979
00:49:09.300 --> 00:49:09.740
Oh.
哦。

980
00:49:09.900 --> 00:49:10.540
Is that a thing?
真有这种说法吗？

981
00:49:10.680 --> 00:49:12.040
Do people carbo-load?
人们真的会进行碳水化合物储备吗？

982
00:49:12.180 --> 00:49:15.540
They do, but like not moments before they run, right?
他们会，但不是在跑步前几分钟，对吧？

983
00:49:15.660 --> 00:49:16.640
I looked it up.
我查过了。

984
00:49:16.760 --> 00:49:18.380
There's two things happening in this moment.
这一刻发生了两件事。

985
00:49:18.560 --> 00:49:20.800
First of all, we have a fakie bag catch.
首先，我们有一个假包的穿帮镜头。

986
00:49:21.300 --> 00:49:22.240
Fakie bag.
假包。

987
00:49:22.540 --> 00:49:23.640
Fakie prop bag.
假道具包。

988
00:49:23.860 --> 00:49:26.820
That bag that Dwight is holding is not a real bag.
德怀特拿的那个包不是真包。

989
00:49:26.820 --> 00:49:28.500
It's one of the ones that doesn't make noise.
它是那种不会发出声音的道具包之一。

990
00:49:28.920 --> 00:49:31.080
And here's the thing about carbo-loading.
关于碳水化合物储备是这样的。

991
00:49:32.520 --> 00:49:36.120
So, guys, this is something that people will do,
伙计们，这是人们会做的事情，

992
00:49:36.160 --> 00:49:40.500
but it's recommended that you do it the week before a high-
但建议你在高强度运动前的一周进行，

993
00:49:40.500 --> 00:49:41.480
The week before.
提前一周。

994
00:49:41.480 --> 00:49:41.860
Yeah.
没错。

995
00:49:41.900 --> 00:49:44.420
A week before a high-endurance activity.
在高耐力活动前的一周。

996
00:49:44.740 --> 00:49:45.300
Yeah.
没错。

997
00:49:45.380 --> 00:49:49.300
The reason why you do this carbo-load the week before
你之所以要在前一周进行碳水化合物储备，

998
00:49:49.300 --> 00:49:53.120
is to boost the glycogen that's stored in your muscles, right?
是为了增加肌肉中储存的糖原，对吧？

999
00:49:53.120 --> 00:49:57.300
So, you can sort of burn on that while you're doing your high-endurance activity.
这样你在进行高耐力活动时，可以消耗这些储备。

1000
00:49:57.300 --> 00:49:59.980
You don't do it minutes before.
你不会在几分钟前才做这件事。

1001
00:50:01.020 --> 00:50:02.320
It's so gross.
太恶心了。

1002
00:50:02.500 --> 00:50:03.160
So gross.
真恶心。

1003
00:50:03.160 --> 00:50:03.920
It's so gross.
太恶心了。

1004
00:50:04.040 --> 00:50:08.240
A lot of people wrote in asking how much fettuccine Steve had to eat.
很多人写信来问史蒂夫到底吃了多少意大利宽面。

1005
00:50:08.440 --> 00:50:09.560
Pretty much none.
基本上没吃。

1006
00:50:09.980 --> 00:50:14.520
I don't know if you noticed, but we cut away before he has to really swallow the fettuccine.
不知道你们有没有注意到，我们在他真正吞下宽面之前就切掉镜头了。

1007
00:50:14.640 --> 00:50:15.480
They had a bucket there.
现场有个桶。

1008
00:50:15.500 --> 00:50:19.580
So, he would shove a bunch in his mouth, and he would spit it out.
所以他会往嘴里塞一大把，然后吐出来。

1009
00:50:19.580 --> 00:50:23.960
Thank God, because it was almost 100 degrees that week every day, and we were outside.
谢天谢地，因为那周每天气温都快到40度了，而且我们还在户外。

1010
00:50:24.180 --> 00:50:26.300
Hot, outside, eating fettuccine.
在户外顶着大热天吃宽面。

1011
00:50:26.500 --> 00:50:26.880
Blah.
呕。

1012
00:50:27.000 --> 00:50:32.940
Can we talk about the ginormous gun that Dwight shoots off to start the race?
我们能聊聊德怀特用来发令起跑的那把巨大的枪吗？

1013
00:50:33.120 --> 00:50:34.800
Not a starter's pistol.
那可不是发令枪。

1014
00:50:34.960 --> 00:50:38.280
An actual gun with actual bullets in it.
那是装了真子弹的真枪。

1015
00:50:38.360 --> 00:50:41.920
Obviously, we shot off blanks, but what the heck?
当然，我们用的是空包弹，但这也太离谱了吧？

1016
00:50:42.080 --> 00:50:42.980
I know.
我知道。

1017
00:50:42.980 --> 00:50:51.500
So, according to Dunderpedia, Dwight uses a 6-inch Colt Anaconda, and it's the same caliber gun used by Dirty Harry.
根据《邓德百科》，德怀特用的是6英寸口径的柯尔特蟒蛇左轮手枪，和《辣手神探》里用的是同款。

1018
00:50:52.460 --> 00:50:53.800
Well, it's ridiculous.
这太荒唐了。

1019
00:50:54.180 --> 00:50:58.800
I believe, though, that he would have some gun that Clint Eastwood fired, like a Dirty Harry gun.
不过我觉得，他确实会用克林特·伊斯特伍德那种枪，比如《辣手神探》里的枪。

1020
00:50:58.980 --> 00:50:59.500
That tracks.
这很符合他的人设。

1021
00:51:00.120 --> 00:51:01.960
It's perfect for his character.
这非常符合他的性格。

1022
00:51:02.240 --> 00:51:03.880
Well, the race is underway.
好了，比赛开始了。

1023
00:51:04.280 --> 00:51:05.960
We fired this gun.
我们开了这把枪。

1024
00:51:06.800 --> 00:51:09.900
Creed, Stanley, and Oscar immediately get into a cab.
克里德、斯坦利和奥斯卡立刻钻进了一辆出租车。

1025
00:51:10.080 --> 00:51:10.320
Yeah.
没错。

1026
00:51:11.420 --> 00:51:12.660
Which is amazing.
这太绝了。

1027
00:51:12.880 --> 00:51:18.680
Stanley says, he will work out today, he will work out a way to avoid running for a stupid cause.
斯坦利说他今天会“锻炼”，他会想办法避免为了这种蠢事去跑步。

1028
00:51:18.940 --> 00:51:19.160
Yeah.
没错。

1029
00:51:19.380 --> 00:51:23.900
They all three have talking heads and deleted scenes that talk about why they're not doing it.
他们三个人都有采访镜头和删减片段，讲了他们为什么不参加。

1030
00:51:24.460 --> 00:51:30.420
Stanley had an alt that said, when he runs, his feet swell up to the size of a pot roast, and you don't want to see that.
斯坦利有个备选镜头说，他一跑步，脚就会肿得像炖肉一样大，你肯定不想看到那个。

1031
00:51:30.940 --> 00:51:31.340
Oh.
噢。

1032
00:51:31.560 --> 00:51:33.140
Well, Angela Martin certainly would not.
安吉拉·马丁肯定不想看。

1033
00:51:33.320 --> 00:51:34.580
She does not like gross feet.
她不喜欢恶心的脚。

1034
00:51:34.840 --> 00:51:35.280
No.
没错。

1035
00:51:35.280 --> 00:51:38.180
Well, we sort of see everybody's approach, right?
我们看到了每个人的应对方式，对吧？

1036
00:51:38.380 --> 00:51:46.740
Like, Andy's going to run, Michael's going really fast, and this is when we find out that Pam and Jim are happily in last place together, just strolling.
比如安迪要跑，迈克尔跑得飞快，然后我们发现帕姆和吉姆正开心地并列最后一名，悠闲地散步。

1037
00:51:47.180 --> 00:51:49.580
Andy's going to draft behind Kevin.
安迪打算跟在凯文后面利用风阻。

1038
00:51:49.580 --> 00:51:54.840
Well, now we have a scene that I love so much, where Jan is handing out water to the runners.
现在有个我非常喜欢的场景，简在给参赛者发水。

1039
00:51:55.200 --> 00:52:07.040
She's somehow moved from the starting line, where she was checking people in, to a new table where she's handing out waters and people haven't even gotten to her yet.
她不知怎么从起跑线——她在那儿负责签到——转移到了一个新的桌子前发水，而选手们甚至还没跑到她那里。

1040
00:52:07.240 --> 00:52:08.700
I found that interesting.
我觉得这很有趣。

1041
00:52:08.940 --> 00:52:09.100
Yeah.
是啊。

1042
00:52:09.100 --> 00:52:11.860
She obviously drove, I guess, to this new spot.
我猜她肯定是开车到了这个新位置。

1043
00:52:13.800 --> 00:52:15.940
Well, Michael refuses to take the water.
迈克尔拒绝接水。

1044
00:52:16.520 --> 00:52:23.840
He explains that rabies victims have to live with an irrational hatred of water, so it's really the least he can do to refuse the water.
他解释说狂犬病患者必须忍受对水的非理性恐惧，所以拒绝喝水是他唯一能做的了。

1045
00:52:24.780 --> 00:52:26.220
Well, I looked it up, Angela.
安吉拉，我查过了。

1046
00:52:26.400 --> 00:52:32.260
You know, last week I told you a lot about rabies and the importance of getting a shot if you're ever bitten by an animal.
你知道，上周我跟你讲了很多关于狂犬病以及被动物咬伤后打疫苗的重要性。

1047
00:52:32.380 --> 00:52:33.920
Hey, I did not look it up.
嘿，我才没查过。

1048
00:52:34.020 --> 00:52:35.500
In fact, I wrote myself a note.
事实上，我给自己写了张便条。

1049
00:52:35.700 --> 00:52:38.320
Ask Jenna, rabies expert, is this true?
问问狂犬病专家珍娜，这是真的吗？

1050
00:52:39.100 --> 00:52:40.540
No, no, you did not.
不，不，你根本没写。

1051
00:52:41.400 --> 00:52:47.220
I have to say I do know a lot more about rabies than I ever thought I would thanks to this podcaSt.
我不得不说，多亏了这个播客，我对狂犬病的了解比我预想的要多得多。

1052
00:52:47.560 --> 00:53:02.160
But this condition is called hydrophobia, and it is an irrational fear of water, and it does present itself in the advanced stages of the disease of rabies.
但这种病症被称为恐水症，这是一种对水的非理性恐惧，它确实会出现在狂犬病的中晚期阶段。

1053
00:53:02.160 --> 00:53:04.300
But here's why.
但原因如下。

1054
00:53:04.600 --> 00:53:11.560
Basically, patients start to fear liquids because it is so painful to swallow.
基本上，患者开始害怕液体，因为吞咽时会感到非常痛苦。

1055
00:53:11.940 --> 00:53:15.600
Like, they don't want to drink or eat anything.
比如，他们不想喝水或吃任何东西。

1056
00:53:15.600 --> 00:53:25.240
So it's not like having water touch them would bother them, but ingesting anything becomes so painful that that's why.
所以并不是说水碰到他们会让他们难受，而是摄入任何东西都会变得非常痛苦，这就是原因所在。

1057
00:53:25.420 --> 00:53:26.380
This is horrible.
这太可怕了。

1058
00:53:26.640 --> 00:53:27.340
This is horrible.
这太可怕了。

1059
00:53:28.660 --> 00:53:30.700
Rabies is a horrible disease.
狂犬病是一种可怕的疾病。

1060
00:53:30.700 --> 00:53:35.820
I cannot stress enough how important it is to get that shot if you are bitten by an animal.
我怎么强调都不为过，如果你被动物咬伤，一定要去打那针疫苗。

1061
00:53:35.820 --> 00:53:42.440
Well, we also didn't mention that Toby ran by and took a swig of water, but threw most of it on Jan.
嗯，我们还没提到托比跑过来喝了一口水，但把大部分都泼在了简身上。

1062
00:53:43.300 --> 00:53:44.680
Yes, this is true.
是的，这是真的。

1063
00:53:45.380 --> 00:53:48.680
Well, Toby's doing great, and we're about to find out why.
好吧，托比做得很好，我们马上就会知道原因了。

1064
00:53:48.800 --> 00:53:49.120
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1065
00:53:49.120 --> 00:53:55.920
Michael is not doing well because of the fettuccine.
迈克尔因为吃了意大利宽面感觉不太好。

1066
00:53:56.380 --> 00:53:56.500
Yeah.
是啊。

1067
00:53:57.220 --> 00:53:59.380
But Dwight tells him he's going to be fine.
但德怀特告诉他会没事的。

1068
00:53:59.380 --> 00:54:03.260
You'll probably still win because he put Imodium in Toby's coffee.
你可能还是会赢，因为他在托比的咖啡里放了易蒙停。

1069
00:54:03.620 --> 00:54:04.700
Michael's so excited.
迈克尔太兴奋了。

1070
00:54:04.860 --> 00:54:05.860
He's like, excellent!
他说，太棒了！

1071
00:54:05.920 --> 00:54:08.620
And then goes, wait, don't you mean X-Lox?
然后又说，等等，你是指X-Lox吗？

1072
00:54:09.060 --> 00:54:09.660
Yes.
是的。

1073
00:54:10.320 --> 00:54:11.880
Dwight has helped Toby.
德怀特帮了托比。

1074
00:54:12.340 --> 00:54:12.480
Yeah.
是啊。

1075
00:54:13.080 --> 00:54:15.140
I want to point something out about this scene.
我想指出关于这个场景的一点。

1076
00:54:15.140 --> 00:54:26.080
During this scene, I swear Michael and Dwight run past Oscar's house, or at least the location that we used for Oscar's house.
在这个场景中，我发誓迈克尔和德怀特跑过了奥斯卡的家，或者至少是我们用作奥斯卡家外景的地方。

1077
00:54:26.640 --> 00:54:36.280
So I looked it up, and yes, we are filming on the same street in Sherman Oaks that has Oscar's house.
所以我查了一下，没错，我们确实是在谢尔曼奥克斯的那条街上拍摄的，那里有奥斯卡的家。

1078
00:54:36.540 --> 00:54:38.140
We filmed there a lot.
我们在那里拍了很多次。

1079
00:54:38.140 --> 00:54:40.080
It was really close to our set.
离我们的片场真的很近。

1080
00:54:40.080 --> 00:54:45.180
And, yeah, I think we run past the location of Oscar's house.
而且，是的，我想我们跑过了奥斯卡家的外景地。

1081
00:54:45.360 --> 00:54:53.640
We filmed there a lot for all those reasons, and also this particular neighborhood in Sherman Oaks has really great, old, old,
因为所有这些原因，我们在那里拍了很多戏，而且谢尔曼奥克斯的这个特定街区确实有一些非常棒的、非常古老的、

1082
00:54:53.740 --> 00:55:00.160
huge trees that might resemble the East Coast more than normally what L.A.
巨大的树木，可能比洛杉矶通常的样子更像东海岸。

1083
00:55:00.220 --> 00:55:00.940
would look like.
看起来是这样。

1084
00:55:01.500 --> 00:55:02.140
Yeah.
是啊。

1085
00:55:02.140 --> 00:55:09.540
Meanwhile, Andy's nipples are starting to chafe, and Creed, Stanley, and Oscar are at like an outside cafe.
与此同时，安迪的乳头开始磨损了，而克里德、斯坦利和奥斯卡正在一家露天咖啡馆。

1086
00:55:09.560 --> 00:55:11.540
They've ordered another round of drinks.
他们又点了一轮饮料。

1087
00:55:11.540 --> 00:55:12.760
I like their style.
我喜欢他们的风格。

1088
00:55:13.240 --> 00:55:13.760
Yes.
是的。

1089
00:55:14.000 --> 00:55:17.700
And Pam and Jim are now going to stop at an estate sale.
帕姆和吉姆现在打算在一家遗产拍卖会停下来。

1090
00:55:17.960 --> 00:55:19.500
I love estate sales.
我喜欢遗产拍卖会。

1091
00:55:19.760 --> 00:55:21.600
My mom, this makes me think of my mom.
我妈妈，这让我想起了我妈妈。

1092
00:55:21.720 --> 00:55:31.380
Whenever we went anywhere, any kind of road trip, if we saw a sign that said yard sale, garage sale, estate sale, my mom would literally pull off the road.
无论我们去哪里，任何形式的公路旅行，如果我们看到写着庭院拍卖、车库拍卖、遗产拍卖的牌子，我妈妈真的会把车开下公路。

1093
00:55:31.380 --> 00:55:41.360
Well, in my sophomore year of college, I got my own apartment, and the summer before I went back to school, my mom took me around to estate sales and garage sales,
嗯，在我大学二年级的时候，我有了自己的公寓，在回学校前的那个夏天，我妈妈带我去了各种遗产拍卖会和车库拍卖会，

1094
00:55:41.400 --> 00:55:51.020
and that's where I bought all of my dishes and my pots and pans and all the stuff I was going to need for my kitchen, and I still have some of that stuff.
我在那里买了我厨房需要的所有盘子、锅碗瓢盆和各种东西，我现在还留着其中一些。

1095
00:55:51.060 --> 00:55:59.800
I still have a baking dish from one of the garage sales that we went to in order to get all my stuff for college.
我还有一个烤盘，就是我们为了凑齐我上大学用的东西时，在其中一个车库拍卖会上买的。

1096
00:55:59.800 --> 00:56:03.240
I still have a little piece of kitchen art.
我还留着一件小小的厨房装饰品。

1097
00:56:03.240 --> 00:56:07.700
It's like a pear and some grapes, and it's like someone made this.
那上面画着一个梨和一些葡萄，看起来像是某人亲手做的。

1098
00:56:07.820 --> 00:56:12.560
Someone made the image and then got a piece of wood and then shellacked over it.
有人制作了图像，然后找了一块木板，在上面刷了虫胶漆。

1099
00:56:12.600 --> 00:56:13.400
Do you know what I mean?
你明白我的意思吗？

1100
00:56:13.780 --> 00:56:14.000
Yes.
明白。

1101
00:56:14.000 --> 00:56:19.540
And it's this sort of kitschy little piece of kitchen art, and I got it at a garage sale.
这是一种俗气的小厨房艺术品，我是从旧货甩卖会上淘来的。

1102
00:56:19.680 --> 00:56:20.800
I love that.
我喜欢这个。

1103
00:56:20.980 --> 00:56:21.860
I did that too.
我也做过同样的事。

1104
00:56:22.440 --> 00:56:28.620
I love estate sales and garage sales because I think they're such a great way to recycle and reuse.
我喜欢遗产拍卖和旧货甩卖，因为我觉得这是循环利用的好方法。

1105
00:56:29.600 --> 00:56:30.260
You know?
你懂吗？

1106
00:56:30.480 --> 00:56:32.400
You don't have to buy everything new.
你不必非得买全新的东西。

1107
00:56:32.680 --> 00:56:35.900
When someone's done with it, use it.
当别人不再需要它时，就接着用吧。

1108
00:56:36.520 --> 00:56:37.600
I love that.
我喜欢这个。

1109
00:56:37.760 --> 00:56:38.480
I love that too.
我也喜欢这个。

1110
00:56:38.540 --> 00:56:41.160
I always love the idea of what that story was.
我总是很喜欢去想象它背后的故事。

1111
00:56:41.280 --> 00:56:45.560
Like what did that green bowl with that one little chip, what was that about?
比如那个带缺口的绿碗，它到底有什么故事呢？

1112
00:56:45.720 --> 00:56:46.880
Now I'm going to have it.
现在它归我了。

1113
00:56:46.880 --> 00:56:48.780
Yes, I agree.
是的，我同意。

1114
00:56:49.100 --> 00:56:56.680
Well, now I love that Ryan and Fancy Corporate calls Dunder Mifflin, and no one is answering.
好吧，现在我喜欢瑞安和“时髦大公司”给邓德·米夫林打电话却没人接的桥段。

1115
00:56:56.680 --> 00:57:01.580
And he gets this message that says, you've reached the offices of Dunder Mifflin Scranton.
他听到一段留言说：您已接通邓德·米夫林斯克兰分公司的电话。

1116
00:57:01.760 --> 00:57:09.580
Currently, the entire staff is out doing the Michael Scott DMSMPMC Rabies Awareness Pro-Am Fun Run Race.
目前，全体员工正在参加迈克尔·斯科特举办的“邓德·米夫林斯克兰分公司狂犬病防治职业业余混合趣味长跑大赛”。

1117
00:57:09.580 --> 00:57:11.740
And then Michael chimes in.
然后迈克尔插话了。

1118
00:57:12.060 --> 00:57:13.380
That's all your voice.
那全是你配的音。

1119
00:57:13.540 --> 00:57:15.720
And Michael chimes in and goes, for the cure.
迈克尔插话说：为了治愈狂犬病。

1120
00:57:15.900 --> 00:57:17.960
And then Pam says, leave a message.
然后帕姆说：请留言。

1121
00:57:21.170 --> 00:57:21.630
Curious.
真有意思。

1122
00:57:21.770 --> 00:57:22.990
I thought it was so funny.
我觉得太搞笑了。

1123
00:57:23.190 --> 00:57:24.890
And Ryan is like, ugh.
瑞安当时就无语了。

1124
00:57:25.270 --> 00:57:30.510
Well, you know Michael was just hovering over Pam's shoulder as she created that outgoing message.
你知道，帕姆录那段语音留言时，迈克尔肯定就在她身后盯着。

1125
00:57:30.790 --> 00:57:31.570
Oh, my goodness.
天哪。

1126
00:57:31.570 --> 00:57:36.070
I would love to have seen how many ways that he made her say it until they got it right.
我真想看看他让帕姆重录了多少遍，才最终录成那样。

1127
00:57:36.070 --> 00:57:36.120
Right.
确实。

1128
00:57:36.930 --> 00:57:41.950
Well, now, lady, Dwight is going to try to sweet talk Angela.
好了，女士，现在德怀特要试着对安吉拉甜言蜜语了。

1129
00:57:42.230 --> 00:57:42.770
He is.
他确实在这么做。

1130
00:57:42.870 --> 00:57:45.630
He runs up next to her, tells her she looks cute as a button.
他跑到她身边，说她看起来可爱极了。

1131
00:57:46.470 --> 00:57:48.470
She's not into it.
她并不领情。

1132
00:57:48.630 --> 00:57:49.550
She doesn't want to hear it.
她根本不想听。

1133
00:57:49.710 --> 00:57:55.050
And there were a lot of things that made this scene a little trickier than it looks.
这场戏拍起来比看起来要棘手得多，有很多因素要考虑。

1134
00:57:55.230 --> 00:57:57.710
We had to deliver all of our dialogue while running.
我们必须一边跑步一边说出所有的台词。

1135
00:57:58.130 --> 00:58:04.850
But we couldn't run so fast that you would never see Steve, who was positioned just behind us in between us.
但我们又不能跑得太快，否则就拍不到史蒂夫了，他当时就站在我们身后中间的位置。

1136
00:58:04.850 --> 00:58:07.050
We couldn't run too close to one another.
我们也不能跑得离彼此太近。

1137
00:58:07.350 --> 00:58:13.270
And we had to pace this out because the camera was getting us in the foreground and Michael in the background.
我们必须控制好节奏，因为摄像机要同时拍到前景的我们和背景里的迈克尔。

1138
00:58:13.910 --> 00:58:15.370
I imagine it was difficult.
我能想象这有多难。

1139
00:58:15.630 --> 00:58:17.530
Also, we only had so much sidewalk.
而且，人行道的空间有限。

1140
00:58:18.110 --> 00:58:21.770
Well, we had a specific place we had to stop, too, on the sidewalk.
没错，我们在人行道上还有特定的停靠点。

1141
00:58:21.810 --> 00:58:25.870
And we had to try to hit that same mark every time because then we see the neighbor.
我们必须每次都精准地停在那个位置，因为接下来我们要看到邻居。

1142
00:58:26.090 --> 00:58:29.590
And we have this great moment that I love where we're like, it's nothing.
我们有一个我很喜欢的精彩瞬间，当时我们说：没什么事。

1143
00:58:29.750 --> 00:58:31.050
And Dwight's like, I'm robbing her.
德怀特却说：我在抢劫她。

1144
00:58:31.110 --> 00:58:31.950
And I'm like, it's fine.
我说：没事的。

1145
00:58:32.010 --> 00:58:33.790
And then at the same time, we're like, it's nothing.
然后我们同时说：真的没什么事。

1146
00:58:33.790 --> 00:58:36.630
And then we go right back to our conversation we were having.
说完我们又立刻回到刚才的话题继续聊。

1147
00:58:37.090 --> 00:58:40.570
Well, we had a fan question from Steph Bailey and Debbie Kay.
我们收到了来自斯蒂芬·贝利和黛比·凯的粉丝提问。

1148
00:58:41.990 --> 00:58:43.410
Kind of more of a statement.
与其说是提问，不如说是一种评价。

1149
00:58:43.650 --> 00:58:46.750
Angela, for not being a runner, you have really great form.
安吉拉，你明明不是跑步爱好者，但你的跑步姿势真的很棒。

1150
00:58:47.270 --> 00:58:48.050
Do I?
是吗？

1151
00:58:49.290 --> 00:58:50.790
I thought so, too.
我也这么觉得。

1152
00:58:50.850 --> 00:58:52.750
I thought you were a very cute runner.
我觉得你是个很可爱的跑步者。

1153
00:58:53.170 --> 00:58:54.070
Well, thank you.
噢，谢谢。

1154
00:58:54.350 --> 00:58:57.090
I mean, I ran cross country in high school, you guys.
我是说，我高中时参加过越野跑，伙计们。

1155
00:58:57.230 --> 00:58:59.710
Maybe somewhere in the back of my brain, it was still there.
也许在我大脑深处的某个地方，还保留着那段记忆。

1156
00:59:00.090 --> 00:59:01.350
Well, there you go.
好吧，原来如此。

1157
00:59:01.350 --> 00:59:06.030
When were you running cross country while also playing basketball and trombone?
你到底是什么时候在打篮球和吹长号的同时还参加越野跑的？

1158
00:59:06.150 --> 00:59:07.150
I don't understand.
我不明白。

1159
00:59:07.530 --> 00:59:08.270
And tennis.
还有网球。

1160
00:59:08.570 --> 00:59:09.510
And I was a cheerleader.
而且我还当过啦啦队长。

1161
00:59:09.730 --> 00:59:11.730
I was busy in high school, Jenna.
我高中时很忙的，珍娜。

1162
00:59:11.950 --> 00:59:15.650
This was my mom's attitude was, if you're busy, you don't have time for trouble.
我妈妈的态度是，只要你忙起来，就没时间惹麻烦了。

1163
00:59:16.770 --> 00:59:18.030
Well, you were busy.
好吧，你确实很忙。

1164
00:59:18.190 --> 00:59:18.990
I was very busy.
我确实非常忙。

1165
00:59:19.850 --> 00:59:22.750
I also want to read you this letter from Patrick Wright.
我还想读给你听这封来自帕特里克·赖特的信。

1166
00:59:22.970 --> 00:59:23.270
Okay.
好的。

1167
00:59:23.270 --> 00:59:26.530
Because I agree with Patrick.
因为我同意帕特里克的观点。

1168
00:59:27.530 --> 00:59:29.270
Here's what Patrick had to say.
这是帕特里克要说的话。

1169
00:59:29.750 --> 00:59:36.050
I really wanted to express my respect for Angela as an actress, especially in this episode.
我真的很想表达我对安吉拉作为一名演员的敬意，特别是在这一集中。

1170
00:59:36.330 --> 00:59:41.130
She is a mixture of tragically funny and also just heartbreaking.
她身上既有一种悲剧性的滑稽感，又让人感到心碎。

1171
00:59:41.130 --> 00:59:45.910
She gives such a fabulous, nuanced performance throughout this entire episode.
她在整集中都贡献了极其精彩、细腻的表演。

1172
00:59:46.250 --> 00:59:50.870
We, as an audience, truly feel for her hurt and anger throughout the story.
作为观众，我们真切地感受到了她在整个故事中受到的伤害和愤怒。

1173
00:59:50.870 --> 00:59:59.050
And my heart broke as she runs away from Dwight with her adoration of the man she loves, but at the same time shattered.
当她带着对所爱之人的崇拜逃离德怀特，却同时又心碎不已时，我的心也跟着碎了。

1174
00:59:59.510 --> 01:00:07.410
The performances from everyone in the cast was brilliant as always, but I felt compelled to single out Angela for her marvelous acting.
剧组中每个人的表演一如既往地出色，但我还是忍不住要特别称赞安吉拉那精湛的演技。

1175
01:00:07.410 --> 01:00:10.590
Aw, that is so nice.
噢，真是太好了。

1176
01:00:10.590 --> 01:00:11.490
Thank you.
谢谢。

1177
01:00:11.790 --> 01:00:13.550
I so appreciate that.
我非常感激。

1178
01:00:14.030 --> 01:00:20.670
We really feel Angela being torn here because Dwight admits he killed sprinkles.
我们真的能感受到安吉拉在这里的挣扎，因为德怀特承认他杀了斯普林克尔斯。

1179
01:00:21.190 --> 01:00:22.570
He mercy killed sprinkles.
他是出于好心才杀了斯普林克尔斯。

1180
01:00:23.530 --> 01:00:31.130
And, you know, Dwight tried to do it in the kindest way and for all the right reasons in his mind, right?
而且，你知道，德怀特自认为是以最仁慈的方式，出于最正当的理由去做的，对吧？

1181
01:00:31.590 --> 01:00:32.050
Yeah.
是的。

1182
01:00:32.050 --> 01:00:36.430
In his perspective and gave her antihistamines until she fell asleep.
在他看来，他给它喂了抗组胺药直到它睡着。

1183
01:00:36.750 --> 01:00:41.170
And then Angela's like, but then she threw them up and she tried to claw her way out.
然后安吉拉说，但它后来把药吐了出来，还试图抓挠着逃出去。

1184
01:00:41.230 --> 01:00:45.410
And she's like, why didn't you talk to me about this first?
她说，你为什么不先跟我商量一下？

1185
01:00:45.850 --> 01:00:48.090
Like, how is this not a conversation?
这怎么就不能商量呢？

1186
01:00:48.310 --> 01:00:54.170
If this was the solution you thought needed to happen, why not talk to me about this?
如果这是你认为必须采取的解决方案，为什么不跟我谈谈？

1187
01:00:55.350 --> 01:01:02.170
And there are sad moments to the scene and then there's these moments where obviously there's a joke written, but I have to say it really earnestly.
这一幕里既有悲伤的时刻，也有一些显然是写好的笑话，但我必须非常认真地说出来。

1188
01:01:02.410 --> 01:01:06.870
Like the cat heaven is a beautiful place, but you don't get there if you're euthanized, you know?
比如猫咪天堂是个美丽的地方，但如果你是被安乐死的，你就去不了那里，你知道吗？

1189
01:01:07.290 --> 01:01:07.690
Yeah.
是的。

1190
01:01:07.690 --> 01:01:19.950
And, but one of the notes Greg gave me was, as you run away, you know, Dwight's like reaching out for you and I say, you don't understand.
而且，格雷格给我的建议之一是，当你跑开时，德怀特在后面伸手想拉你，而我说，你不明白。

1191
01:01:20.830 --> 01:01:23.850
And I kind of start to cry as I run away.
我跑开的时候开始哭了起来。

1192
01:01:23.910 --> 01:01:31.130
And he said, you know, what Dwight isn't getting is that this is unforgivable for you.
他说，你知道，德怀特不明白的是，这对你来说是不可原谅的。

1193
01:01:31.710 --> 01:01:32.270
Yeah.
是的。

1194
01:01:32.270 --> 01:01:37.650
And you love this man, but he has severed this bond.
你爱这个男人，但他已经切断了这段羁绊。

1195
01:01:37.870 --> 01:01:40.150
You don't think you can be with him anymore.
你觉得你再也不能和他在一起了。

1196
01:01:40.290 --> 01:01:43.330
But Dwight doesn't know that yet, but you know it.
但德怀特还不知道这一点，而你已经知道了。

1197
01:01:44.090 --> 01:01:53.450
Well, I've had this happen in relationships where you're dating and you're so in love and the relationship is just all promise and optimism.
嗯，我在恋爱中也遇到过这种情况，你们正在约会，深爱着对方，这段关系充满了希望和乐观。

1198
01:01:54.050 --> 01:02:07.330
And then something happens and the person reacts or acts in such a way that you realize there is a fundamental difference of values.
然后发生了一些事，对方的反应或行为让你意识到你们之间存在根本的价值观差异。

1199
01:02:08.150 --> 01:02:08.290
Yeah.
是的。

1200
01:02:08.450 --> 01:02:11.890
And, and she knows it and she knows she can't see him the same way.
而且，她心里很清楚，她再也无法用同样的眼光看待他了。

1201
01:02:12.050 --> 01:02:17.790
And it will take a very, very, very long time as we know for her to forgive him.
而且正如我们所知，她要原谅他还需要很长、很长、很长的时间。

1202
01:02:18.650 --> 01:02:18.850
Yeah.
是啊。

1203
01:02:20.350 --> 01:02:21.910
Well, guess what?
嗯，你猜怎么着？

1204
01:02:22.990 --> 01:02:24.690
Jim and Pam bought a lamp.
吉姆和帕姆买了一盏灯。

1205
01:02:25.070 --> 01:02:26.670
Just the base of a lamp.
只是个灯座。

1206
01:02:27.190 --> 01:02:27.710
Yeah.
是啊。

1207
01:02:27.770 --> 01:02:30.230
It was $8 and now Jim gets to carry it.
才8美元，现在吉姆得负责拎着它。

1208
01:02:31.110 --> 01:02:33.530
It's an odd choice, this green lamp.
这盏绿色的灯，选择真是奇怪。

1209
01:02:34.990 --> 01:02:38.750
It looks like two octopus tentacles are holding hands or something.
看起来就像两根章鱼触手在牵手什么的。

1210
01:02:38.930 --> 01:02:40.350
I don't know what's happening with it.
我不知道这玩意儿到底是什么鬼。

1211
01:02:40.570 --> 01:02:45.130
How does Jim feel about Pam's taste if this is the lamp she wanted to buy?
如果这就是帕姆想买的灯，吉姆会对她的品味作何感想？

1212
01:02:45.390 --> 01:02:48.350
Is he concerned about moving in together one day?
他会担心以后搬到一起住吗？

1213
01:02:48.670 --> 01:02:50.210
Maybe sharing a house?
也许是合租一栋房子？

1214
01:02:50.210 --> 01:02:51.530
This lamp is not great.
这灯真不怎么样。

1215
01:02:51.750 --> 01:02:55.370
But also, Michael is really struggling.
但与此同时，迈克尔真的很挣扎。

1216
01:02:55.690 --> 01:02:57.270
Phyllis and Bob pass him up.
菲利斯和鲍勃都超过了他。

1217
01:02:57.390 --> 01:02:59.030
I mean, he's laying on the ground.
我是说，他都躺在地上了。

1218
01:02:59.090 --> 01:03:00.630
His lips are all white.
他的嘴唇都发白了。

1219
01:03:00.630 --> 01:03:01.710
He doesn't look good.
他看起来状态很差。

1220
01:03:01.990 --> 01:03:04.230
He doesn't look like he's going to make it.
他看起来快撑不下去了。

1221
01:03:04.890 --> 01:03:07.710
But in the meantime, Toby wins the race.
但与此同时，托比赢得了比赛。

1222
01:03:08.610 --> 01:03:08.730
Yeah.
是啊。

1223
01:03:08.910 --> 01:03:12.930
And I thought it was so perfect that Kelly is at the finish line, like on her phone.
我觉得凯莉在终点线那儿玩手机的样子真是太绝了。

1224
01:03:13.790 --> 01:03:14.210
Yes.
没错。

1225
01:03:16.230 --> 01:03:17.910
And he's like, where are we?
然后他问，我们在哪儿？

1226
01:03:18.070 --> 01:03:21.050
And she's like, we're about five kilometers from the office.
她说，我们离办公室大概还有五公里。

1227
01:03:21.710 --> 01:03:24.730
And Toby's like, why didn't Michael make it a circle?
托比就问，迈克尔为什么不设计成环形路线？

1228
01:03:24.990 --> 01:03:25.170
No.
没门。

1229
01:03:25.470 --> 01:03:26.570
He couldn't have made it easy.
他才不会让事情变得简单呢。

1230
01:03:26.830 --> 01:03:27.930
He made it a straight line.
他偏要设计成直线。

1231
01:03:28.250 --> 01:03:29.510
Well, it's interesting.
嗯，这很有意思。

1232
01:03:29.870 --> 01:03:37.370
So that spot where they are is pretty much right outside of our real office, actually.
其实他们所在的位置就在我们真实办公室的外面。

1233
01:03:37.650 --> 01:03:40.130
That was on Sadekoy Street where we shot.
那是我们在萨德科伊街拍摄的。

1234
01:03:40.130 --> 01:03:42.870
So we actually were very, very close.
所以我们其实离得很近很近。

1235
01:03:43.070 --> 01:03:46.170
Like we just walked back to set at the end.
就像最后我们直接走回片场一样。

1236
01:03:46.390 --> 01:03:46.590
Yeah.
是啊。

1237
01:03:46.810 --> 01:03:50.270
So we actually did end very close to our office.
所以我们最终结束的地方离办公室确实很近。

1238
01:03:50.650 --> 01:03:56.850
You know, I guess it's interesting because Pam, like I think she's going to give Michael
你知道，我觉得挺有意思的，因为帕姆，我以为她会给迈克尔

1239
01:03:56.850 --> 01:03:59.990
a pep talk, but she's like, no, you don't got this.
打气，但她说，不，你做不到。

1240
01:04:00.550 --> 01:04:06.050
It's more like Pam's house of like, there's other people that are better at helping people.
这更像是帕姆的风格，就是说，有其他人比你更擅长帮助别人。

1241
01:04:06.170 --> 01:04:07.770
Why don't you just let this one go?
你为什么不干脆放弃呢？

1242
01:04:07.770 --> 01:04:10.950
And then Michael's like, you don't know me.
然后迈克尔说，你不了解我。

1243
01:04:11.150 --> 01:04:12.950
You've just seen my penis.
你只是看过我的阴茎而已。

1244
01:04:13.450 --> 01:04:19.770
And somehow Pam not cheering him on makes him cheer himself on.
不知怎么的，帕姆没有为他加油，反而让他自己为自己加油了。

1245
01:04:19.910 --> 01:04:24.550
And he has this talking head where he's like, finishing that 5K was the hardest thing I've
他有个采访镜头，他说，跑完这5公里是我这辈子

1246
01:04:24.550 --> 01:04:25.290
ever had to do.
做过最难的事情。

1247
01:04:25.450 --> 01:04:31.390
I ate more fettuccine Alfredo and drank less water than he ever has in his entire life.
我吃的阿尔弗雷多奶油宽面比我这辈子任何时候都多，喝的水却比任何时候都少。

1248
01:04:31.950 --> 01:04:33.470
This was so funny to me.
这对我来说太搞笑了。

1249
01:04:33.470 --> 01:04:39.830
He slowly makes his way across the finish line and I caught a palm tree.
他慢慢挪过终点线，我还抓拍到了一棵棕榈树。

1250
01:04:41.050 --> 01:04:41.570
Yeah.
是啊。

1251
01:04:42.090 --> 01:04:43.030
Did you see it?
你看到了吗？

1252
01:04:43.510 --> 01:04:44.450
Yes, I did.
看到了。

1253
01:04:44.710 --> 01:04:44.930
Yeah.
没错。

1254
01:04:45.650 --> 01:04:47.570
39 minutes, 46 seconds.
39分46秒。

1255
01:04:47.810 --> 01:04:48.930
Palm tree alert.
棕榈树预警。

1256
01:04:49.690 --> 01:04:50.510
We did not.
我们没看到。

1257
01:04:50.550 --> 01:04:52.050
I guess we didn't paint that one out.
看来我们没把那棵树修掉。

1258
01:04:52.230 --> 01:04:52.430
Yeah.
是啊。

1259
01:04:52.430 --> 01:04:56.550
I'm sure there are others along the way because, you know, we're filming outside so much.
我相信沿途肯定还有别的，毕竟我们在户外拍了那么多戏。

1260
01:04:56.790 --> 01:05:03.610
But he finally makes it across the finish line and Jim gives him the lamp as a trophy and he
但他最终冲过了终点线，吉姆把那盏灯当成奖杯给了他，然后他

1261
01:05:03.610 --> 01:05:04.210
pukes.
吐了。

1262
01:05:05.130 --> 01:05:05.270
Yeah.
是啊。

1263
01:05:06.450 --> 01:05:08.610
Probably some kind of mushroom soup.
可能是某种蘑菇汤吧。

1264
01:05:08.830 --> 01:05:10.870
Oh, it looked, it looked gross.
噢，看起来，看起来真恶心。

1265
01:05:11.130 --> 01:05:12.130
It looked, it was so gross.
看起来，真是太恶心了。

1266
01:05:12.190 --> 01:05:13.110
It looks so gross.
看起来真恶心。

1267
01:05:13.290 --> 01:05:15.150
And he let it just dribble down his chin.
而且他就任由呕吐物顺着下巴流下来。

1268
01:05:15.350 --> 01:05:17.790
I'm like, wipe that off your face.
我当时心想，快把脸上擦干净啊。

1269
01:05:18.150 --> 01:05:18.970
So gross.
太恶心了。

1270
01:05:18.970 --> 01:05:26.370
Well, this episode ends with Michael in the hospital and Meredith has wheeled herself in
这集结尾是迈克尔在医院，梅雷迪思坐着轮椅

1271
01:05:26.370 --> 01:05:28.330
to his room to visit him.
进了他的病房探望他。

1272
01:05:28.830 --> 01:05:29.090
Yes.
没错。

1273
01:05:29.310 --> 01:05:34.870
There is a deleted scene that Michael checked himself into the hospital for dehydration
有一个删减片段是迈克尔因为脱水住进了医院，

1274
01:05:34.870 --> 01:05:39.490
and he requested his childhood pediatrician come visit him.
他还要求他儿时的儿科医生来探望他。

1275
01:05:40.130 --> 01:05:42.770
And his pediatrician is a very elderly man.
而他的儿科医生是一位非常年迈的老人。

1276
01:05:43.790 --> 01:05:47.350
And he's saying, you know, Michael doesn't really need to be in the hospital.
医生说，迈克尔其实根本没必要住院。

1277
01:05:47.350 --> 01:05:48.890
He got a little dehydrated.
他只是有点脱水而已。

1278
01:05:49.310 --> 01:05:52.170
Really, this all could have been solved with a bottle of water.
说真的，这一切本可以靠一瓶水解决的。

1279
01:05:52.590 --> 01:05:56.670
But, and then as he's talking, Michael's like, where's my lollipop?
但是，就在医生说话的时候，迈克尔问，我的棒棒糖呢？

1280
01:05:57.070 --> 01:05:58.270
He like gives him his.
医生就把他的棒棒糖给了他。

1281
01:05:58.290 --> 01:05:58.890
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

1282
01:05:58.910 --> 01:06:02.050
So is that why he has a lollipop in this scene with Meredith?
所以这就是他在和梅雷迪思那场戏里拿着棒棒糖的原因吗？

1283
01:06:02.230 --> 01:06:07.370
Yes, because his pediatrician stopped by and checked in on him and gave him a lollipop.
是的，因为他的儿科医生顺道来看他，给了他一根棒棒糖。

1284
01:06:08.550 --> 01:06:12.590
Well, the lollipop leads us to a very cringy final moment.
嗯，这根棒棒糖引出了一个非常尴尬的结局时刻。

1285
01:06:12.810 --> 01:06:13.110
Yes.
没错。

1286
01:06:13.110 --> 01:06:20.590
Which is that Michael is sucking on the lollipop and he suggests that they share it.
那就是迈克尔在吮吸棒棒糖，然后他提议两人分享。

1287
01:06:21.650 --> 01:06:31.190
So he hands it to Meredith who then sort of puts it in her mouth and then she offers it back to Michael
于是他递给了梅雷迪思，梅雷迪思把它放进嘴里，然后又递回给迈克尔，

1288
01:06:31.190 --> 01:06:33.630
and he says, nah, no, I'm good.
结果他说，不了，不用了，我不用了。

1289
01:06:33.810 --> 01:06:33.930
I'm good.
我不用了。

1290
01:06:34.130 --> 01:06:34.770
I'm good.
我不用了。

1291
01:06:35.230 --> 01:06:37.790
Well, we had some mail.
我们收到了一些来信。

1292
01:06:38.630 --> 01:06:41.730
From Eliza Jarvis and Natalie Benari.
来自伊丽莎·贾维斯和娜塔莉·贝纳里。

1293
01:06:42.330 --> 01:06:47.830
Please tell me the lollipop Michael shares with Meredith is switched out before they share it.
请告诉我，迈克尔和梅雷迪思分享的那根棒棒糖在分享前换过了。

1294
01:06:48.250 --> 01:06:49.870
Did they really share it?
他们真的分享了同一根吗？

1295
01:06:50.550 --> 01:06:53.110
Guys, I wondered the same thing.
伙计们，我也纳闷过同样的问题。

1296
01:06:53.110 --> 01:06:56.190
When I watched this scene, there is no cut.
我看这场戏的时候，镜头没有剪辑。

1297
01:06:56.390 --> 01:07:04.470
It's a one-er shot of Steve taking the lollipop out of his mouth and handing it to Kate.
这是一个长镜头，史蒂夫从嘴里拿出棒棒糖递给了凯特。

1298
01:07:05.890 --> 01:07:07.810
So we asked Kate about it.
所以我们问了凯特这件事。

1299
01:07:08.010 --> 01:07:10.090
We had to ask her about it.
我们必须得问问她。

1300
01:07:11.090 --> 01:07:14.990
And she said they did not rinse it off.
她说他们根本没冲洗过。

1301
01:07:15.190 --> 01:07:20.330
She also said Steve improvised that in the moment and she just went with it.
她还说那是史蒂夫当时即兴发挥的，她只是顺着演了下去。

1302
01:07:21.170 --> 01:07:26.690
But yeah, and I think that's why you see her pause a second.
不过确实，我觉得这就是为什么你会看到她停顿了一秒。

1303
01:07:27.250 --> 01:07:32.450
I think you are watching Kate, the person, decide if she's going to do this.
我想你看到的是凯特本人在纠结要不要这么做。

1304
01:07:32.590 --> 01:07:35.150
She's like, am I going to do this?
她当时大概在想，我要这么做吗？

1305
01:07:37.050 --> 01:07:38.610
But brilliant ending.
但结局真的很棒。

1306
01:07:38.990 --> 01:07:40.190
Good for you, Kate.
干得好，凯特。

1307
01:07:40.770 --> 01:07:43.210
Way to really go for it on the show.
在节目里真是豁出去了。

1308
01:07:43.390 --> 01:07:47.130
She said she got a thrill out of doing her own sort of stunts.
她说她很享受亲自完成那种特技表演的过程。

1309
01:07:47.410 --> 01:07:49.270
So yeah, she's brave.
所以没错，她很勇敢。

1310
01:07:49.270 --> 01:07:55.210
And you know, there was a Dwight deleted talking head that I think would have come after this
而且你知道，德怀特有一个被删减的采访片段，我觉得应该是在这之后出现的，

1311
01:07:55.210 --> 01:08:00.230
where it's really, it kind of broke my heart, where he talks about forgiveness
那个片段真的让我很心碎，他谈到了宽恕，

1312
01:08:01.330 --> 01:08:07.530
and what it is to forgive someone and that he hopes that his friend will forgive him.
谈到了宽恕一个人意味着什么，以及他希望他的朋友能原谅他。

1313
01:08:08.050 --> 01:08:13.130
Because if Meredith can forgive Michael for hitting her with a car,
因为如果梅雷迪思能原谅迈克尔开车撞她，

1314
01:08:13.830 --> 01:08:16.230
maybe his friend will be able to forgive him.
也许他的朋友也能原谅他。

1315
01:08:16.330 --> 01:08:17.430
And he's hopeful.
他对此充满希望。

1316
01:08:17.430 --> 01:08:21.570
I know, it made me sad.
我知道，这让我很难过。

1317
01:08:22.110 --> 01:08:22.870
Yeah.
是啊。

1318
01:08:23.930 --> 01:08:28.250
Well, I think that finishes out Fun Run.
好吧，我想《趣味长跑》这一集就讲到这里了。

1319
01:08:28.490 --> 01:08:29.770
We did a Fun Run.
我们完成了一次趣味长跑。

1320
01:08:29.990 --> 01:08:38.050
Thank you guys so much for joining us for the Michael Scott DM SMP MC Rabies Awareness Pro-Am Fun Run Race.
非常感谢大家参加我们的“迈克尔·斯科特DM SMP MC狂犬病意识职业业余混合趣味长跑比赛”。

1321
01:08:38.610 --> 01:08:39.550
For the cure.
为了治愈狂犬病。

1322
01:08:40.550 --> 01:08:42.130
We'll be back next week.
我们下周见。

1323
01:08:42.970 --> 01:08:47.600
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.
感谢收听《办公室女士》。

1324
01:08:47.860 --> 01:08:51.820
Office Ladies is produced by Earwolf, Jenna Fisher, and Angela Kinsey.
《办公室女士》由Earwolf、珍娜·费舍和安吉拉·金赛制作。

1325
01:08:52.000 --> 01:08:53.520
Our producer is Cody Fisher.
我们的制作人是科迪·费舍。

1326
01:08:53.720 --> 01:08:55.680
Our sound engineer is Sam Kiefer.
我们的音响工程师是萨姆·基弗。

1327
01:08:55.840 --> 01:08:57.900
And our associate producer is Ainsley Bubiko.
我们的助理制作人是安斯利·布比科。

1328
01:08:58.140 --> 01:09:00.780
Our theme song is Rubber Tree by Creed Bratton.
我们的主题曲是克里德·布拉顿演唱的《橡胶树》。

1329
